 Rubrik, Inc. in October 2014. The company was incorporated in 2013 and is based in Palo Alto, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bipul  Sinha | Co-Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $347K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $67K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $87K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Rubrik, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $21.8B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +48% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +101.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Gross margins of 75% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $253M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -22.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -20.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 25% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 413% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation",